    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "CHINA AIRWAYS FEDERAL INC. U. S. A.\nCABLE ADDRESS: \"PACAMAIR\"\n51 CANTON ROAD\nSHANGHAI\nPersonal\nMr.\nS.1P. Morgan,\nPacific American\nAirways,\n135 East Forty-second St.,\nNew York City, N.Y.\nDear Mr. Morgan,\n29 August, 1935\nI like Chinese chow and frequently work\nout with the sticks but there are times when it is a bit trying.-\nI am enclosing an invitation from Mr.\nM.Y. Tang and a menu of the dinner.\nYou will note item four\non\nthe menu.\nIt is considered polite\namong Chinese to use your own\nsticks (which, of course, you constantly put in your mouth) to\nremove choice\nmorseis Irom the center, common source of supply.\necause I don't like to eat food which others have deposited witł\ntheir chop sticks on my plate I am always extremely polite and\nusually manage to beat them to the draw. That system worked very\nwell the other night until the fourth item on the menu came along.\nThen, while I was\nwaiting on Mrs. Tang,\nthe Chinese lady on my\nleft\nwaited on me by depositing on my plate the foot of a chicken,\na great delicacy, which I had to devour or lose a lot of face,\nin fact, be quite insulting.\nSo far as flavor, for which chicken\ndoncernea - would much rather work out on an\nınner tube, which, rüns about as much but under more sanitary con-\nditions than a Chinese chicken.\nWhen I was in Kweiyang with Communists\nattacking the city I worried a lot as to whether I should let\nthe airplane fly away without me so as to see Chiang Kai Shek or\ngo with the plane.\nFinally, when the missionaries decided to\nleave I made up my mind that if the missionaries wouldn't stick\nit out for Jesus that there was no particular point in my sticking\nit\nar neck out for Juan.\nI'm glad that the Communists were eventu-\nally defeated but I'm still sorry that that chicken was.\nSincerely,\nH.M. Bixby\nUSE\nSAVE\nTIME"
